# L §6.4, §8.3 item 9 (tally 2.1.6, P29 on T's SR-T1 of #75), a twin: with no `when` and no `where`, every key of
# days is an instance, and its day is its key, so load sees that top[2025-12-30] books before 2026-01-01 and refuses
# topup at load, as #75 made it. Both 2.1.6 refcores refuse it so.
=== base.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-02
  start 2025-12-30
  end 2026-01-05

source s "s"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input from_day: date

input early: date

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-05)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  from_day = 2026-01-01
  early = 2025-01-01
  opening[konto] = 10.00 PLN at 2025-12-30 start
=== scen.tally
scenario topup over hh
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

move top[d in days]: transfers
  on d
  leg cash from world to konto amount 1.00 PLN

ask q_top: bal(konto, 2026-01-05) in topup
=== expect q_top
scenario topup: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO move top of topup books on 2025-12-30, before 2026-01-01 (scen.tally:5)
warning: WARN-UNREAD input early is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input from_day is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD place world is read by nothing
